  "term": "pertussis",
  "definition": "Pertussis is a highly contagious respiratory illness marked by a long-lasting coughing illness with repeated coughing fits. It can lead to serious complications, especially in infants and young children, and it remains a concern when vaccination is incomplete or immunity has declined.",
